You already answered that yourself in your first sentence. They are hard
because they are weak characters in the beginning. Ask yourself how your
game might have evolved with 9-11 less points of AC. And what happened
if your character (then without the MR from the GDSM) would have stumbled
into the polytrap (instead of your pet) thereby probably also ruining any
hard acquired body armour and cloak instead of gaining a powerful pet, in
addition to the AC boost (which is crucial for arcs!) and MR.

BTW; my first played game on NAO was a gnomish healer, and I ascended it.
(I don't recall whether I had some lucky event, or just had no nasty RNG.)
Though because of that single data point I wouldn't call them easy, rather
this class is generally considered to be from the hard ones. Meanwhile, I
played 16 healers (9 gnomish) and ascended 6 (just 2 gnomish ones). More
data points, more appropriate results.

